From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chatkord <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tap: lend the host each received frame's bytes, and decode in
 the host

The crate decodes a received frame itself and cannot hand its bytes out or decode on VA-API.
Measured: on Machine B a 4K60 stream decodes at 3.8 ms a picture on the GPU, against about
30 ms in the engine's software decoder.

The engine's own encoded sink (AddEncodedSink) lends the host each frame the frame buffer
releases, in decode order and never past a lost reference. Stand-in H.264 and AV1 decoders
sit in the engine for the frame buffer to feed; the host asks for a key frame. The stand-in
is process-wide (decode_in_host).

